  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Host Information — Hardware", "technique": "T1082", "what_happened": "At 2027-07-14 09:12:05 CEST, Sysmon Event ID 1 on agent WIN-ITOPS-184 (10.108.57.184) logged a process-create for C:\\Windows\\System32\\wbem\\WMIC.exe with data.win.eventdata.commandLine 'wmic cpu get name' under user CORP\\t.helpdesk. ~40 seconds later a second WMIC.exe process-create fired with commandLine 'wmic memorychip get capacity'. Both spawned from a cmd.exe parentImage. This is the hardware-enumeration sub-technique of Gather Victim Host Information — CPU model and installed-RAM capacity are exactly the facts an adversary needs to confirm bare-metal vs virtualized and size a payload.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule fired on Sysmon Event ID 1 where data.win.eventdata.image ends with WMIC.exe AND data.win.eventdata.commandLine matches the hardware-query pattern (*cpu get*, *memorychip get*). rule.mitre.id T1082 attached automatically.", "first_seen": "2027-07-14T09:12:05+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Host Information — Firmware", "technique": "T1082", "what_happened": "At 09:18:33 CEST (~6-minute pause after the hardware queries — consistent with an operator reading output before continuing), a third WMIC.exe process-create on WIN-ITOPS-184 logged commandLine 'wmic bios get smbiosbiosversion'. Reading the SMBIOS / firmware version is the firmware sub-technique — it tells the adversary which BIOS/UEFI persistence paths and firmware CVEs are viable on this exact machine.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event ID 1, data.win.eventdata.image ends with WMIC.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine wildcard *bios get*. Same agent.name WIN-ITOPS-184, same user CORP\\t.helpdesk, same cmd.exe parentImage as step 1 — confirms a single continuing session, not unrelated noise.", "first_seen": "2027-07-14T09:18:33+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Host Information — Client Configuration", "technique": "T1082", "what_happened": "At 09:24:51 CEST, Sysmon Event ID 1 on WIN-ITOPS-184 logged C:\\Windows\\System32\\systeminfo.exe with an empty/standard commandLine 'systeminfo', followed ~90 seconds later by C:\\Windows\\System32\\gpresult.exe with commandLine 'gpresult /r'. systeminfo dumps the full OS build, hotfix/patch list and domain role; gpresult /r dumps the applied Group Policy set. Together they give the adversary the OS-version + patch-level intelligence needed to pick a working kernel/privilege-escalation exploit, plus the policy posture of the endpoint.", "chain_reason": "Two Sysmon Event ID 1 records on agent.name WIN-ITOPS-184: data.win.eventdata.image ends with systeminfo.exe and gpresult.exe respectively, under user CORP\\t.helpdesk. The rule grouped them with steps 1-2 because they share host + user + the recon command-pattern within a 25-minute window.", "first_seen": "2027-07-14T09:24:51+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Host Information — Security Tool Awareness", "technique": "T1082", "what_happened": "At 09:31:10 CEST, Sysmon Event ID 1 on WIN-ITOPS-184 logged a PowerShell process-create C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe with data.win.eventdata.commandLine 'powershell Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_Product' and ~50 seconds later a second PowerShell process-create with commandLine 'powershell Get-Service WinDefend,Sense'. Enumerating installed products (Win32_Product) plus the state of the Microsoft Defender (WinDefend) and Defender-for-Endpoint (Sense) services is the software-inventory + security-tool-awareness sub-technique — the adversary is checking the installed-software surface AND whether EDR is running before deciding how loud the next stage can be.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event ID 1, data.win.eventdata.image ends with powershell.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine wildcard *Get-WmiObject* and *Get-Service*WinDefend*. Same agent.name WIN-ITOPS-184, same user CORP\\t.helpdesk — fourth distinct host-recon category from one session, which is what escalated the correlated alert to 'sustained host profiling'.", "first_seen": "2027-07-14T09:31:10+0200"}
  ],
